# MuffMode Cursor Rule

Read and follow `AGENTS.md` in the repository root. It is the canonical agent guide for Cursor, VS Code Copilot, Codex, and other coding agents.

This Cursor rule is intentionally only an adapter. If a convention should apply outside Cursor, update `AGENTS.md` first.

## Bootstrap

- Check `git status --short` before editing; this repo is often mid-refactor.
- Treat existing edits, deletes, moves, and untracked files as user work.
- Keep changes scoped; no drive-by refactors or generated-output churn.
- Prefer `rg` / `rg --files` for discovery.
- Do not commit, amend, push, or open PRs unless explicitly asked.

## Current Layout

- Server game code: `src/sgame/`
- MuffMode server modules: `src/sgame/muffmode/`
- Client/HUD code: `src/cgame/`
- Shared types/helpers: `src/shared/`
- Host tests: `tests/host/`
- Canonical CI/local scripts: `scripts/ci/`

If older docs mention `src/muffmode/` or `src/g_local.h`, verify the live split-tree path with `rg`. `GAMEMOD_VERSION` currently lives in `src/sgame/g_local.h`.

## Architecture

- Keep upstream-style Quake II files as thin hooks; put feature bodies in MuffMode modules.
- New server features usually belong in `src/sgame/muffmode/mm_<feature>.{h,cpp}`, with API in the header, inclusion from `src/sgame/muffmode/muffmode.h`, and entries in `src/game.vcxproj` plus `.filters`.
- Keep command wrappers in `src/sgame/core/commands.cpp` thin: `Cmd_*_f` delegates to `MM_Cmd*`.
- Store player prefs in `client_config_t` / `client->sess.pc`, not raw userinfo.
- Register server cvars in `src/sgame/core/runtime.cpp`, declare externs in `src/sgame/g_local.h`, and document user-facing cvars in `docs/configuration-reference.md`.

## Build And Test

From repo root, in a Visual Studio 2022 developer shell:

```powershell
./scripts/ci/build-msbuild.ps1 -Configuration Release -Platform x64 -TreatWarningsAsErrors
```

Fast host tests:

```powershell
./scripts/ci/run-host-tests.ps1 -Configuration Release -Platform x64
```

See `docs/build-guide.md` and `docs/hardening-guide.md`.

## Commits

- Only commit when explicitly asked.
- One-line subject, repo style: `area: what changed; bump X.Y.Z.` when a version bump is part of the work.
- Never amend pushed commits; never skip hooks unless asked.

## Docs And Versioning

- Player-facing commands -> `docs/player-guide.md`
- Cvars -> `docs/configuration-reference.md`
- Implementation-facing changes normally need a grouped `Unreleased` row in `docs/changelog.md`.
- For release-bound version work, keep root `VERSION` and `GAMEMOD_VERSION` in `src/sgame/g_local.h` exactly aligned. Do not change `GAMEVERSION`.
